

!.env.example
# Benchmark results (stale data — regenerate with bench/benchmark.py)
# Build artifacts
# Config files (regenerable) — never commit real credentials
# Consent scope files (per-target, not for distribution)
# Historical documentation (archived, not for distribution)
# Learning notes (proprietary — not for distribution)
# Live-infrastructure probe scripts (hit real Supabase/Firebase — not for CI)
# OS / editor junk
# PUSH-TO-100 benchmark target installs (heavy deps, regenerable)
# Scratch / temp
# Structured log output (created at import by titan/core/logger.py)
# Third-party tool clones (embedded git repos — kept local, not vendored)
# Track E — signed authorization documents + operator keypair: NEVER commit.
# arena runtime (fight record regenerates each run)
# lab runtime uploads (webshell channel validation)
# regenerating fight artifacts (blue homework + batch lifecycle)
# scratch / backups
# secrets — never commit
